#. Tag: title
#: kdeapps.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; applications"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kppp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many &kde; users report problems using &kppp;. But before you complain about "
"&kppp;, make sure you have already checked the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Can you dialup to your <acronym>ISP</acronym> without using &kppp;? If you "
"cannot, then perhaps &kppp; is not the culprit after all."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Have you gone through the &kppp; documentation at least three times and "
"followed its instructions and trouble-shooting suggestions?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kppp; documentation can be accessed through the <application>&kde; Help "
"Center</application>. Last, but not least, the &kppp; homepage is at <ulink "
"url=\"http://ktown.kde.org/~kppp/\">http://ktown.kde.org/~kppp/</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now, if you still encounter problems, here's what might help you solve them:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdeapps.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I change the &MTU; setting in &kppp;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open up the &kppp; dialog box and select <guibutton>Setup</guibutton>. "
"Choose an existing account and click <guibutton>Edit</guibutton>, or "
"<guibutton>New</guibutton> to create a new dialup account. Select the "
"<guilabel>Dial</guilabel> tab and click <guibutton>Arguments</guibutton>. "
"Type what you want to change in the Argument textbox (&eg; <userinput>mtu "
"296</userinput>) and click <guibutton>Add</guibutton>. When you are "
"satisfied, click <guibutton>Close</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To check whether the options <quote>took</quote>, do one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In a terminal window, run <userinput><command>/sbin/ifconfig</command> ppp0</"
"userinput> and look at the reported &MTU; in the output. It should match "
"your request."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Add <option>debug</option> and <option>kdebug</option> (each on a separate "
"line) to your <filename>/etc/ppp/options</filename> file and restart your "
"&PPP; session. You will find debugging messages in <filename>/var/log/"
"messages</filename>, including &MRU; and &MTU; settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want, the &MRU; and &MTU; settings can be added to the "
"<filename>options</filename> file, one complete setting per line, no quotes "
"or dashes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdeapps.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kppp; connects at a slower speed than normal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following might do the trick:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "Try executing <command>setserial spd_hi</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default &MTU; value is 1500, which maybe too large for a dialup "
"connection. Try changing it to a smaller value like <userinput>296</"
"userinput> or <userinput>576</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check in your <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/"
"config</filename> for the <filename>kppprc</filename>. Ensure the correct "
"modem speed is actually defined there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "&konsole;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdeapps.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I page-up or page-down?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use <keycombo action=\"simul\"> &Shift;<keycap>Page Up</keycap></keycombo> "
"and <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>Pg Dn</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdeapps.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How do I perform a simple <quote>copy</quote> from &konsole; to anything "
"else?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I do a <command>ls</command>, first I select with the mouse the desired "
"text, press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo>, "
"then I make the target application active, point the mouse to the relevant "
"part and press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>V</keycap></"
"keycombo>. Alternatively, highlight the text by dragging with the &LMB; down "
"and paste by clicking with the &MMB; (or both buttons if you are using a 2 "
"button mouse with 3 button emulation)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kdeapps.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why can't &konsole; find the <quote>9x15</quote> and the 2 <quote>console</"
"quote> bitmap fonts installed with &kde;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<application>FontConfig</application> must find the three fonts installed "
"in: <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/fonts</"
"filename>. If the &kde; install does not install these fonts in a directory "
"that already exists (&eg; <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/share/fonts</"
"filename>) then you must add this directory to the configuration file "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/etc/fonts/local.conf</filename>. This should "
"be the first line after <quote>&lt;fontconfig&gt;</quote>. For example: "
"<programlisting>\n"
"&lt;fontconfig&gt;\n"
"&lt;dir&gt;/usr/kde3/share/fonts&lt;/dir&gt;\n"
"&lt;/fontconfig&gt;\n"
"</programlisting> After adding the directory, run (as root): "
"<userinput><command>fc-cache</command> -v</userinput> and check that it "
"found the directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kmail;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kdeapps.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmail; has its own home page at <ulink url=\"http://kmail.kde.org\">http://"
"kmail.kde.org</ulink> where a <acronym>FAQ</acronym> is available."
msgstr ""
